:"2026-11-08T00:00:16Z","text":"Peter Brian Hegseth (born June 6, 1980) is an American government official, U.S. Army veteran, and former television personality who has been serving as the 29th United States secretary of defense since 2025.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384164618:0"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:24Z","text":"Pete Hegseth was born on 6 June 1980 in Minneapolis.","cites":["wd:Q7172014:P569","wd:Q7172014:P19"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:32Z","text":"Educated at Forest Lake Area High School, Princeton University and John F. Kennedy School of Government.","cites":["wd:Q7172014:P69:Q5469002","wd:Q7172014:P69:Q21578","wd:Q7172014:P69:Q49127"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:38Z","text":"Worked for Fox News, in Arlington County.","cites":["wd:Q7172014:P108:Q186068","wd:Q7172014:P937:Q107126"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:44Z","text":"14 awards on record, among them Bronze Star Medal and Joint Service Commendation Medal.","cites":["wd:Q7172014:P166:Q928314","wd:Q7172014:P166:Q15821622"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:51Z","text":"Known for American Crusade and The War on Warriors.","cites":["wd:Q7172014:P800:Q131459708","wd:Q7172014:P800:Q131926991"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:58Z","text":"The Guardian headlined it: “Hakeem Jeffries supports impeachment of Pete Hegseth: ‘He has got to go’”","cites":["news:guardian:ef5d60457aa6"]},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:01:09Z","text":"Sources: The Guardian, Wikipedia articles, Wikimedia pageviews and Wikidata. Every caption links to the evidence it rests on.","cites":["wiki:rev:1384164618:198","views:en:Pete_Hegseth:30d","wd:Q7172014:P569"]}],"time":"story","chapters":[{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:00Z","title":"What happened"},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:24Z","title":"Born"},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:32Z","title":"A life across the globe"},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:43Z","title":"Recognition"},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:00:57Z","title":"In the news"},{"t":"2026-11-08T00:01:08Z","title":"Sources"}],"panels":[{"id":"life","t":"2026-11-08T00:00:33Z","until":"2026-11-08T00:00:43Z","title":"A lif